# Vendored from tibrezus/llm-wiki-core — the repo-map action (RIG producer).
# Byte-equivalent copies; the CI vendor-sync step (ci.yml, rig-emit job)
# checks out THIS sha and fails on any drift. Sync = cp the files below,
# update this pin, run make test-rig-emit, regenerate extensions fixtures.
upstream: https://github.com/tibrezus/llm-wiki-core
sha: 8e0feabd852ff515b137ce83f74f6bfa1fef3bf9
path: .github/actions/repo-map
files:
  emit-rig.py
  rig/builder.py rig/calls.py rig/clones.py rig/db.py rig/fitness.py
  rig/__init__.py rig/model.py rig/symbols.py rig/validator.py
  rig/extractors/base.py rig/extractors/cargo.py rig/extractors/cmake.py
  rig/extractors/generic.py rig/extractors/go.py rig/extractors/__init__.py
  rig/extractors/npm.py rig/extractors/python.py rig/extractors/zig.py
# harmostes-owned, NOT vendored: rig-brief.py, rig-to-c4.py, rig-emit.sh,
# test_validator.py, test_brief.py
# Upstream .py files deliberately NOT vendored (the vendor-sync step asserts
# upstream's .py set minus the vendored set never exceeds this list — an
# addition upstream is a sync DECISION):
#   rig-query.py   — the image's query surface is the pi extension
#                    (extensions/rig-query) + rig-brief.py; a Python CLI
#                    would be a third query path for the same data
#   rig-to-c4.py   — harmostes-owned copy exists (evolved separately)
#   rig-fitness.py — the fitness MODULE ships (rig/fitness.py); the CLI
#                    wrapper has no in-image consumer (wiki-lint candidate)
#   build-wiki-pages.py — llm-wiki docs-site builder, no harmostes role
# ONE vendor patch on top (severity pin, rhesadox#1864): rig/validator.py
#   upstream bytes | vendor-patch.py stdin>stdout  ==  vendored rig/validator.py
# The CI vendor-sync step applies this script before the byte-compare.
